IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er2-common`
IMPORT `er2-family-supplement`

-- Tests of er2-family-supplement (regulation 34). Every expected value is written by hand from the figures printed in lines 523 to 527 and 537
-- to 538 of the Regulations' raw file and from the text of the subsection named beside it; none is read back from the encoding.
-- One #ASSERT per line. Table 5 columns used (1 child / 2 / 3 / top-up per additional child / age supplement per child under 7):
--   under $20,921           31.30 / 58.70 / 86.10 / 27.45 / 4.15
--   $20,921 to $21,250      31.25 / 58.60 / 86.00 / 27.40 / 4.10
--   $21,251 to $21,500      28.50 / 53.60 / 78.80 / 25.60 / 3.85
--   $22,751 to $23,000      17.15 / 32.70 / 48.60 / 17.40 / 2.60
--   $25,751 to $25,921       0.70 /  1.40 /  2.10 /  0.95 / 0.15
-- Table 7 (a child 12 to 15 / a child 16 or 17): under $20,921 2.25 / 3.60; $20,921 to $21,250 2.20 / 3.55.

§ `Regulation 34(1), (2) - meanings`

#ASSERT     `reg 34(1) cohabitating spouse or common-law partner` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 34(1) cohabitating spouse or common-law partner` FALSE)
#ASSERT     `reg 34(2) the Canada child benefit is deemed to be an overpayment under Subdivision a.1 of Division E of Part I of the Income Tax Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 34(2) the Canada child benefit is deemed to be an overpayment under Subdivision a.1 of Division E of Part I of the Income Tax Act` FALSE)
#ASSERT `regulation 34(2.1) - repealed, and therefore not encoded` EQUALS "(2.1) [Repealed, SOR/99-290, s. 1]"

§ `Regulation 34(3), (4) - when the rate is increased`

-- The month preceding the Sunday of the week: a week whose Sunday is 1 March 2026 (Wednesday 4 March is in it) has February 2026 before it
`er2 test February 2026` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28)
`er2 test December 2025` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2025 12 1), (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31)
`er2 test January 2026` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31)
`er2 test January 2025` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31)
`er2 test February 2024` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2024 2 1), (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT `reg 34(3) the month preceding the Sunday of the week` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) EQUALS `er2 test February 2026`
#ASSERT `reg 34(3) the month preceding the Sunday of the week` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS `er2 test February 2026`
-- Wednesday 7 January 2026 is in the week of Sunday 4 January: the month before is December 2025
#ASSERT `reg 34(3) the month preceding the Sunday of the week` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 7) EQUALS `er2 test December 2025`
-- Saturday 28 February 2026 is in the week of Sunday 22 February: the month before is January 2026
#ASSERT `reg 34(3) the month preceding the Sunday of the week` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28) EQUALS `er2 test January 2026`
-- Saturday 1 March 2025 is in the week of Sunday 23 February 2025: January 2025
#ASSERT `reg 34(3) the month preceding the Sunday of the week` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) EQUALS `er2 test January 2025`
-- Tuesday 5 March 2024 is in the week of Sunday 3 March 2024: February 2024 has 29 days
#ASSERT `reg 34(3) the month preceding the Sunday of the week` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 5) EQUALS `er2 test February 2024`
#ASSERT     `reg 34(3) the claimant's rate of weekly benefits for the week is to be increased by a family supplement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 34(3) the claimant's rate of weekly benefits for the week is to be increased by a family supplement` FALSE)
#ASSERT     `reg 34(4) the claimant's rate of weekly benefits for the week shall not be increased` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 34(4) the claimant's rate of weekly benefits for the week shall not be increased` FALSE)

§ `Regulation 34(5) - the table`

-- the band edges (whole dollars): under $20,921 is the first band; $20,921 starts the second; $21,250 ends it; $21,251 starts the third
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 20920 1 0 EQUALS JUST 31.3
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 20921 1 0 EQUALS JUST 31.25
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 21250 1 0 EQUALS JUST 31.25
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 21251 1 0 EQUALS JUST 28.5
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 20000 1 0 EQUALS JUST 31.3
-- two and three children in the second band
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 21000 2 0 EQUALS JUST 58.6
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 21000 3 0 EQUALS JUST 86
-- three children in the third band
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 21400 3 0 EQUALS JUST 78.8
-- four children at $23,000 (band $22,751 to $23,000): 48.60 for three, 17.40 for the fourth
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 23000 4 0 EQUALS JUST 66
-- of them two under 7: plus 2 x 2.60
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 23000 4 2 EQUALS JUST 71.2
-- five children: 48.60 + 2 x 17.40
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 23000 5 0 EQUALS JUST 83.4
-- the last band, $25,751 to $25,921: one child under 7 is 0.70 + 0.15
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 25921 1 1 EQUALS JUST 0.85
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 25751 3 0 EQUALS JUST 2.1
-- two children under 7 in the first band: 58.70 + 2 x 4.15
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 20000 2 2 EQUALS JUST 67
-- not covered: above the table; an income with cents (no band for it); no child; more children under 7 than children; a negative count
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 25922 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 21250.5 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 21000 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 21000 1 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the family supplement` 21000 2 (0 MINUS 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the table rows themselves
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the table row for the family income` 20921 EQUALS JUST (`er2 Family supplement for an income range` OF 31.25, 58.6, 86, 27.4, 4.1)
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the table row for the family income` 25921 EQUALS JUST (`er2 Family supplement for an income range` OF 0.7, 1.4, 2.1, 0.95, 0.15)
#ASSERT `reg 34(5) the table row for the family income` 26000 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 34(6) - the ceiling`

#ASSERT `reg 34(6) the percentage of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings that the family supplement shall not exceed` 1997 EQUALS JUST (10%)
#ASSERT `reg 34(6) the percentage of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings that the family supplement shall not exceed` 1998 EQUALS JUST (15%)
#ASSERT `reg 34(6) the percentage of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings that the family supplement shall not exceed` 1999 EQUALS JUST (20%)
#ASSERT `reg 34(6) the percentage of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings that the family supplement shall not exceed` 2000 EQUALS JUST (25%)
#ASSERT `reg 34(6) the percentage of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings that the family supplement shall not exceed` 2026 EQUALS JUST (25%)
#ASSERT `reg 34(6) the percentage of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings that the family supplement shall not exceed` 1996 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the ceiling: the lesser of the supplement and the percentage of the weekly insurable earnings
#ASSERT `reg 34(6) the family supplement after the ceiling` 66 (25%) 200 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `reg 34(6) the family supplement after the ceiling` 66 (25%) 400 EQUALS 66
#ASSERT `reg 34(6) the family supplement after the ceiling` 66 (25%) 264 EQUALS 66
#ASSERT `reg 34(6) the family supplement after the ceiling` 66 (10%) 400 EQUALS 40

§ `Regulation 34(7) - the additional amount for older children`

-- args: day the benefit period was established, the week, (5) results in a reduction, family income, children 12 to 15, children 16 or 17
-- benefit period established 1 March 1999, week of 1 August 1999 (not before it), reduction, income $21,000: 2.20 + 3.55
#ASSERT `reg 34(7) the additional amount for the week` (YearMonthDay 1999 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 8 1) TRUE 21000 1 1 EQUALS JUST 5.75
#ASSERT `reg 34(7) the additional amount for the week` (YearMonthDay 1999 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 8 1) TRUE 21000 2 0 EQUALS JUST 4.4
#ASSERT `reg 34(7) the additional amount for the week` (YearMonthDay 1999 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 8 1) TRUE 20000 1 1 EQUALS JUST 5.85
-- the week falls before 1 August 1999; or the benefit period was established on 1 August 1999; or no reduction: (7) adds nothing
#ASSERT `reg 34(7) the additional amount for the week` (YearMonthDay 1999 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 7 31) TRUE 21000 1 1 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 34(7) the additional amount for the week` (YearMonthDay 1999 8 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 9 5) TRUE 21000 1 1 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 34(7) the additional amount for the week` (YearMonthDay 1999 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 9 5) FALSE 21000 1 1 EQUALS JUST 0
-- children under 12 are not in the table
#ASSERT `reg 34(7) the additional amount for the week` (YearMonthDay 1999 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 8 1) TRUE 21000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- it applies but the income has no band
#ASSERT `reg 34(7) the additional amount for the week` (YearMonthDay 1999 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 8 1) TRUE 26000 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 34(7) the additional amount for the week` (YearMonthDay 1999 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 8 1) FALSE 26000 1 1 EQUALS JUST 0

§ `Regulation 34 - the increase of the rate of weekly benefits`

-- args: established (3), spouse also paid an increased rate (4), family income, children with the benefit, of them under 7, weekly insurable earnings,
-- day the benefit period was established, the week, (5) results in a reduction, children 12 to 15, children 16 or 17
-- 4 children, 2 under 7, income $23,000: 71.20; ceiling 25% of 400 is 100, so 71.20; benefit period of 2026, so (7) adds nothing
#ASSERT `reg 34 the amount by which the rate of weekly benefits for the week is increased` TRUE FALSE 23000 4 2 400 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 71.2
-- weekly insurable earnings of 200: the ceiling is 50
#ASSERT `reg 34 the amount by which the rate of weekly benefits for the week is increased` TRUE FALSE 23000 4 2 200 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 50
-- a 1998 benefit period, week of 5 September 1999, reduction: 31.25 (ceiling 15% of 300 is 45) + 2.20 for one child 12 to 15
#ASSERT `reg 34 the amount by which the rate of weekly benefits for the week is increased` TRUE FALSE 21000 1 0 300 (YearMonthDay 1998 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 9 5) TRUE 1 0 EQUALS JUST 33.45
-- the same with weekly insurable earnings of 100: ceiling 15% of 100 = 15, then the addition 2.20 on top of the ceiling (fork F16)
#ASSERT `reg 34 the amount by which the rate of weekly benefits for the week is increased` TRUE FALSE 21000 1 0 100 (YearMonthDay 1998 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 9 5) TRUE 1 0 EQUALS JUST 17.2
-- not established: no increase; the spouse's benefits are increased too: no increase
#ASSERT `reg 34 the amount by which the rate of weekly benefits for the week is increased` FALSE FALSE 23000 4 2 400 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `reg 34 the amount by which the rate of weekly benefits for the week is increased` TRUE TRUE 23000 4 2 400 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- not covered: the family income is above the table; a benefit period established before 1997
#ASSERT `reg 34 the amount by which the rate of weekly benefits for the week is increased` TRUE FALSE 30000 1 0 400 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 34 the amount by which the rate of weekly benefits for the week is increased` TRUE FALSE 21000 1 0 400 (YearMonthDay 1996 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1997 3 4) FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
